============================================================
SUMMARY: Direction vs Norm Independence
============================================================

1. Direction Isolation (post_ln2 layer):
   - Direction only R²: 0.1787
   - Norm only R²: 0.8812
   -> Direction carries 101.0% of position info
   -> Norm carries 497.8% of position info

2. After Orthogonalizing Norm Direction:
   - R² dropped from 0.1770 to 0.1012
   - Variance removed: 0.85%

3. PCA Analysis:
   - Best PC for position: PC8 (r=-0.0834)
   - Best PC for norm: PC13 (r=-0.0699)

============================================================
CONCLUSIONS
============================================================
-> Norm is DOMINANT for position encoding
-> Position and Norm are encoded in DIFFERENT principal components
   (They provide partially independent information)

